      "title": "Use of Proceeds",
      "excerpt": "Use of proceeds We estimate that the net proceeds to us from this offering and, if it is consummated, the concurrent private placement will be approximately $\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003million, or approximately $\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003million\nif the underwriters exercise their option to purchase additional shares in full, after deducting the underwriting discounts and commissions, placement agent fees and estimated offering and private placement expenses payable by us. We currently\nintend to use the net proceeds from this offering, and, if consummated, the concurrent private placement, and if consummated, S-8 Table of Contents the concurrent convertible notes offering, together with our existing cash, cash equivalents and short- term investments, to primarily fund our ongoing and planned clinical trials advancing RAP-219, for other research and\ndevelopment, and for working capital and general corporate purposes. See the section ",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Risk Factors",
      "excerpt": "RISK FACTORS Investing in our common stock involves a high degree of risk. Before you decide to invest in our common stock, you should\ncarefully consider the risks and uncertainties described below and in Part I, Item 1A. \u201cRisk Factors\u201d in our Annual Report on Form 10-K for the year ended December\u00a031, 2025, our Quarterly\nReports on Form 10-Q for the quarters ended March\u00a031, 2026 and June\u00a030, 2026, and any of our subsequent Quarterly Reports on Form 10-Q and Current Reports on\nForm 8-K, as applicable, together with all other information contained in this prospectus supplement, the accompanying prospectus and in our filings with the SEC that we have incorporated by reference in this\nprospectus supplement and in any free writing prospectus that we have authorized for use in connection with this offering. If any of the following risks actually occurs, our business, financial condition or res",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Dilution",
      "excerpt": "DILUTION If you invest in our common stock in this offering, your ownership interest will be diluted immediately to the extent of the\ndifference between the public offering price per share of our common stock and the as adjusted net tangible book value per share of our common stock after this offering. As of June\u00a030, 2026, we had net tangible book value of approximately $422.5\u00a0million, or $8.81\u00a0per share of our\ncommon stock, based upon 47,955,079 shares of our common stock outstanding as of that date (which includes 317,771\u00a0shares of unvested restricted common stock outstanding as of June\u00a030, 2026). Historical net tangible book value per share is\nequal to our total tangible assets, less total liabilities and deferred offering costs, divided by the number of outstanding shares of our common stock. Without taking into account any other changes in our historical net tangible book value afte",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Dividend Policy",
      "excerpt": "DIVIDEND POLICY We have never declared or paid cash dividends on our capital stock. We currently plan to retain all of our future earnings, if\nany, to finance the operation, development and growth of our business. Therefore, we do not expect to pay any cash dividends on our common stock in the foreseeable future. Payment of future dividends, if any, will be at the discretion of our board\nof directors and will depend on our financial condition, results of operations, capital requirements, restrictions contained in current or future financing instruments, provisions of applicable law and other factors the board deems relevant. Our\nability to pay dividends on our common stock may be restricted by the terms of any of our future indebtedness. S-21 Table of Contents THE CONCURRENT CONVERTIBLE NOTES OFFERING Concurrently with this offering, we are offering, pursuant to a separate prospectus sup",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    }
